# VS Code REST Client / Visual Studio .http file.
# Use the bootstrap admin configured via user-secrets (see README).
# Credentials are read from backend/src/Omnichannel.Api/.env (git-ignored), e.g.:
#   BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL=...
#   BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=...
# Never put a real credential in this file.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
@email = {{$dotenv BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@password = {{$dotenv BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}

### Health (anonymous)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Login
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### Current user
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Validation error (400 ProblemDetails)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": ""
}

### ---- Channel product mappings (task 014) and realtime / dashboard (task 015) ----
# Run "Login" first: the requests below take the token from its response. Ids are placeholders: copy them from the
# responses of "Channels" and "Products" (or set the variables here). No secrets in this file.
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}
@channelId = 0199a1b0-0000-7000-8000-000000000002
@productId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@channelProductId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Channels (ids of website / pos / digital-platform)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/channels
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Products (pick a productId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/products?pageSize=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Mappings of a channel (search: SKU, product name, external product id, external SKU)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/channels/{{channelId}}/products?page=1&pageSize=20&sortBy=sku
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Map a product on the channel (Manager/Admin) - 201 with syncTaskId
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/channels/{{channelId}}/products
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "productId": "{{productId}}",
  "externalProductId": null,
  "externalSku": "WEB-0001"
}

### One mapping (the Location of the 201)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/channels/{{channelId}}/products/{{channelProductId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Change external ids / deactivate a mapping (Manager/Admin)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/channels/{{channelId}}/products/{{channelProductId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "externalProductId": null,
  "externalSku": "WEB-0002",
  "status": "Active"
}

### Stock-sync tasks of the channel
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/processing/tasks?taskType=StockSync&channelId={{channelId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dashboard summary (default range: the last 24 hours)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dashboard summary for a range (at most 92 days)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/dashboard/summary?from=2026-10-01T00:00:00%2B07:00&to=2026-10-02T23:59:59%2B07:00
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Realtime hub: negotiate (what a SignalR client does first). 401 without a token.
# A browser passes the token as ?access_token=... on the hub's requests; here the header is used so that no token ends up
# in a URL of this file.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/hubs/notifications/negotiate?negotiateVersion=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
